[h1]Tribute Adjust — Live 0%–200% Subject & Tributary Income Control[/h1]

[quote]
[b]"Want your colonial nations, vassals, or tributaries to pay 150%—or give a loyal march a 50% tax break—without editing game files or restarting?"[/b]
[/quote]

Whether you are reigning over a continent-spanning [b]HRE vassal swarm[/b], managing the [b]Celestial Empire of Ming's tributary sphere[/b], or building a [b]tall trade & subject empire[/b], EU4's vanilla tribute math can feel rigid. Stack too many late-game modifiers and your subjects spiral into bankruptcy; leave them at default and rich subjects barely contribute to the imperial treasury.

[b]Tribute Adjust[/b] ([code]dev.foch.eu4-tribute-adjust[/code]) puts a live, precision fiscal dial directly in your hands. Scale the [b]final monthly vassal income share[/b] and [b]annual tributary payouts[/b] anywhere from [b]0% (complete tax holiday)[/b] to [b]200% (double extraction)[/b] in real time—without editing [code]vassal_income[/code] or [code]tribute_income_modifier[/code] script files and without restarting your campaign!

[hr][/hr]

[h2]Why You'll Love It (Core Features)[/h2]

[list]
[*][b]Live Control Panel ([code]Ctrl+Shift+T[/code] / [code]tribute-panel[/code]):[/b]
Adjust tribute scaling from [b]0% to 200%[/b] on the fly with clean graphical sliders. Changes save atomically to [code]tribute-config.json[/code] and hot-reload inside EU4 within [b]250 ms[/b]—zero game restarts required.

[*][b]3-Tier Precision Control (Replaces, Never Stacks Unpredictably!):[/b]
Fine-tune your empire's tax code across three clear priority tiers. Higher-priority rules [b]cleanly replace[/b] lower ones instead of multiplying together into runaway numbers:
  [list]
  [*][b]Tier 1 — Individual Country Tag Overrides ([code]tag_overrides[/code] / [code]tag_percent[/code]):[/b] Target specific subjects by 3-letter tag (e.g., [code]{"FRA": 150, "MUG": 50}[/code] to squeeze an unruly France at 150% while granting loyal Mughals or Korea a 50% subsidy rate).
  [*][b]Tier 2 — Per-Subject-Kind ([code]vassal_percent[/code] / [code]kind_percent[/code]):[/b] Set distinct rates by subject type ([code]vassal[/code], [code]tributary[/code], [code]tributary_state[/code], [code]eyalet[/code], [code]core_eyalet[/code], [code]daimyo_vassal[/code], or custom overhaul types), automatically following [code]copy_from[/code] parent inheritance down to [code]default[/code].
  [*][b]Tier 3 — Global Baseline ([code]global_percent[/code]):[/b] Your empire-wide default percentage ([code]0[/code]–[code]200%[/code], default [code]100%[/code]) when no tag or kind rule matches.
  [/list]

[*][b]Instant Master Switch ([code]enabled[/code]):[/b]
Want to compare your custom tax rates against vanilla numbers? Flip [code]enabled = false[/code] in the panel to drop every subject back to [b]100% vanilla passthrough[/b] immediately, then toggle it back on whenever you are ready.

[*][b]Final-Payout Scaling (No Modifier Bloat):[/b]
Scales the final tribute payout and monthly vassal transfer directly rather than mutating script modifiers. Keep your subjects solvent in 1750 or fund your mega-projects when you need ducats, monarch points, and manpower most.
[/list]

[hr][/hr]

[h2]Built for Major Overhaul Mods[/h2]

Unlike static script tweaks that hardcode vanilla's default subject list, Tribute Adjust dynamically inspects your active playset's [code]common/subject_types/*.txt[/code] files:
[list]
[*][b]Dynamic Subject Discovery:[/b] Automatically follows [code]copy_from[/code] inheritance chains and respects mod [code]descriptor.mod[/code] [code]replace_path[/code] rules in your exact playset load order.
[*][b]Ready for Total Conversions:[/b] Built with [b]Anbennar[/b], [b]Ante Bellum[/b], [b]Europa Expanded[/b], and custom subject overhauls in mind—supporting up to [b]32,767 country tag slots[/b] and displaying the full indented [code]copy_from[/code] subject-type tree right inside [code]tribute-panel[/code].
[/list]

