[h2]Simple 3-Step Installation via Foch[/h2]

[b]Why is Foch required?[/b]
Standard EU4 Clausewitz script files cannot scale individual subject payouts dynamically at runtime or open a live 0-200% slider panel without reloading the game. [b]Foch[/b] runs Tribute Adjust ([code]dev.foch.eu4-tribute-adjust[/code]) in an [b]isolated runtime layer[/b]. It [b]never alters or dirties your Steam EU4 installation files[/b] and can be toggled on or off in one command. This Steam Workshop item is the companion mod: its decision only opens a note. The native plugin does the scaling.

[b]Step 1 — Install Foch over HTTPS (China-mirror friendly, no gh CLI)[/b]
Install the [code]foch[/code] program over HTTPS. Cargo and uv honor a China mirror (Tsinghua TUNA, Aliyun, rsproxy, or a ByteDance PyPI/crates mirror) and do not need the GitHub [code]gh[/code] CLI:
[code]
# Option A: Cargo. Point crates.io at a mirror first if you need one.
cargo install foch-cli --locked

# Option B: uv. A PyPI mirror in your environment is used automatically.
uv tool install foch
[/code]
You can also download the Windows x64 release zip over HTTPS from GitHub Releases, or from a mirror of that zip, and put [code]foch.exe[/code] on PATH.

[b]Step 2 — Package the plugin, then import it[/b]
Subscribe to this Workshop companion. From a checkout, one command writes a fresh package directory and refuses an existing directory or symlink. The package contains [code]foch-plugin.toml[/code], [code]foch_eu4_tribute.dll[/code], [code]signatures/signatures-1.37.5.toml[/code], [code]LICENSE[/code], SHA-256 checksums, and [code]tribute-panel.exe[/code] when that tool has been built. [code]foch plugin import[/code] reads that directory locally and does not call [code]gh[/code]:
[code]
python mods/tribute-adjust/tools/package.py target/tribute-adjust-pkg
foch plugin import target/tribute-adjust-pkg
foch plugin enable dev.foch.eu4-tribute-adjust --playset default
[/code]
[i][code]foch plugin install[/code] is Foch's command for a published plugin release. In this Foch build that download still runs [code]gh release download[/code], so it needs the GitHub CLI and is not the mirror-friendly path. Tribute Adjust does not use that command: install Foch over HTTPS, package this plugin, then [code]foch plugin import[/code].[/i]

[b]Step 3 — Launch EU4 via Foch and press Ctrl+Shift+T[/b]
Start the game through Foch's isolated runtime launcher and open the slider panel anytime:
[code]
foch plugin launch --playset default
[/code]
You can also configure baseline values in [code]foch-plugin.toml[/code] ([code]enabled[/code], [code]global_percent[/code], [code]vassal_percent[/code], [code]tag_overrides[/code]) or edit [code]tribute-config.json[/code] with the [code]tribute-panel[/code] window while playing.

[hr][/hr]

[h2]Compatibility, Current Status & Honest FAQ[/h2]

[b]Q: Which EU4 version is supported? Will a game update break my save?[/b]
[b]A:[/b] Tribute Adjust strictly targets [b]EU4 [code]1.37.5[/code] (Windows x64 Steam build)[/b]. On startup, the plugin verifies the exact executable signature of [code]eu4.exe[/code]. If Paradox releases a new patch or you launch an unsupported binary, the plugin cleanly [b]refuses to load ([code]REFUSED[/code])[/b] and leaves the game untouched—it will [b]never[/b] blindly hook, crash to desktop, or corrupt your save files.

[b]Q: What is already verified vs. still pending live end-to-end verification before the 1.0 release?[/b]
[b]A:[/b] We believe in 100% transparency with players:
[list]
[*][b]Verified Today:[/b] Exact [code]1.37.5[/code] executable signature matching and safe host activation/refusal; baseline tributary scaling (verified in live Ming 1444 sessions across 100%, 50%, and 0% rates); baseline vassal income share scaling (verified in live England/Wales sessions); offline playset [code]common/subject_types[/code] & [code]copy_from[/code] tree discovery; and [code]tribute-panel[/code] slider GUI atomic hot-reloading (250 ms debounce).
[*][b]Pending Full Live Verification Before 1.0:[/b]
  [list]
  [*]Live in-game regression of province-based subject Tag resolution on the monthly vassal income path is passed in synthetic memory tests and queued for final pre-1.0 live regression (if a subject tag is not resolved on that path, it safely falls back to the [code]"vassal"[/code] / global percentage without crashing).
  [*]In-game runtime hooks currently query the [code]"tributary"[/code] and [code]"vassal"[/code] channels directly while playset-root handoff to the in-process hook is finalized; to tune specific custom sub-kinds ([code]eyalet[/code], [code]core_eyalet[/code], [code]appanage[/code], etc.) during live play right now, use [b]Per-Tag Overrides ([code]tag_overrides[/code] / [code]tag_percent[/code])[/b].
  [*]If you launch the game with the vassal baseline set to [code]0%[/code] and no tag overrides configured, raising the rate above [code]0%[/code] mid-session requires a game restart.
  [/list]
[/list]

[b]Q: Does this work in Ironman or Multiplayer?[/b]
[b]A:[/b]
[list]
[*][b]Ironman & Achievements:[/b] Because EU4 is launched with a native runtime plugin via Foch, [b]Steam Ironman achievements are disabled[/b] while the plugin is active.
[*][b]Multiplayer:[/b] Supported when [b]all players in the lobby[/b] launch EU4 via Foch with the [b]exact same [code]tribute-config.json[/code] / percentage settings[/b]. Mismatched tribute multipliers between host and clients will cause an economy OOS (Out of Sync).
[/list]
